<p>The Trump administration is asking a US trade court to pause the next stage of litigation over whether it must repay importers for tariffs the US Supreme Court struck down last week. The administration says the refund process is complicated and will take time. The Justice Department said it will not ask the Supreme Court to rehear the case, even as President Trump criticized the ruling publicly and signaled opposition to large-scale refunds. The decision has already set off a rush of claims—described in coverage as more than 2,000 lawsuits—by companies seeking reimbursement for duties paid under the now-invalid tariffs. That sets up what multiple outlets call a legally fraught, potentially long fight in the US Court of International Trade. For readers outside the US, the immediate story is less about any single court date and more about the uncertainty this adds to US trade policy and cross-border supply chains, even as the ruling shows US institutions can still put firm legal guardrails on executive economic actions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/P8hQyBMvbAAbgxV-xNfHhsKTfCb-uQJYA0JOzaucDydRIM_wPTqWaHsCHoLSzn2Er4lrUUQnxB_g7EyJdfmi9V0tQns1igITvHZ_SIbEvOspahpVErOXWLpRc2ERycbQ6tACrkswR3w9-MIgxINdo2iI8VLsVH0hwD_CuV6_pMFadDQHRkntOmmKFdAz-aLpQlZOvdSLYzDNP5i1DyqoAcqKDcm9NYf3iYd49cj2qihBIu-4LOGvwFU' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Refund scale: Some analyses cited in coverage put total refund claims as high as $175 billion, raising the stakes for businesses and for the US budget.</li><li>Who is suing: Coverage says many of the companies bringing these tariff suits are smaller businesses, not just multinationals.</li><li>Delay request: Justice Department filings ask for up to a four-month pause before refund-focused proceedings resume at the US Court of International Trade.</li><li>Rule-of-law framing: Commentary cast the ruling as a win for the rule of law—tariffs function like taxes and need proper legal authority—while warning it could increase near-term uncertainty.</li><li>Corporate claimants: Companies lining up for reimbursement reportedly include FedEx, and other firms mentioned in coverage include Costco, Toyota, Goodyear and Alcoa.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Department of Justice: In court documents, the department said the refund mechanics “will take time” and said it does not plan to ask the Supreme Court to rehear the case. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/27/trump-tariff-refunds'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>President Trump: After the Supreme Court ruling, President Trump criticized the decision publicly and signaled opposition to refunds, with coverage describing a legal fight ahead. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-signals-opposition-to-tariff-refunds-hinting-at-legal-war-to-come'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Importing businesses: Importers have filed or are preparing claims seeking reimbursement for duties they paid under tariffs the Supreme Court said were imposed illegally. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/27/trump-tariff-refunds'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Commentary writers: Analysis pieces framed the ruling as a rule-of-law win but warned it could bring short-term uncertainty as the White House looks for alternative tariff authorities and litigation grows. (<a href='https://theweek.com/business/economy/return-of-tariff-turmoil-trump'>The Week</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/economy-trade-business/article/3344958/us-government-seeks-delay-tariff-refund-court-hearing-faces-above-2000-lawsuits'>US government seeks delay on tariff refund court hearing, faces above 2,000 lawsuits</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/27/trump-tariff-refunds'>Trump administration warns tariff refund process ‘will take time’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/business/economy/return-of-tariff-turmoil-trump'>Supreme Court tariff ruling: a welter of new uncertainties</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-faces-2000-tariff-lawsuits-following-supreme-court-loss'>Trump faces 2,000 tariff lawsuits following Supreme Court loss</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-administration-seeks-delay-in-tariff-refunds-battle/article70687021.ece'>Trump administration seeks delay in tariff refunds battle</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>